    "category" : "CodeStyle",
    "subCategory" : null,
    "title" : "Prefer indexed access operator [] for map element access or insert",
    "description" : "Enforces the use of the indexed access operator [] instead of explicit get() or put() method calls for accessing or inserting elements in maps or lists.",
    "explanation" : "# ExplicitCollectionElementAccessMethod\n\nIn Kotlin functions `get` or `set` can be replaced with the shorter operator — `[]`,\nsee [Indexed access operator](https://kotlinlang.org/docs/operator-overloading.html#indexed-access-operator).\nPrefer the usage of the indexed access operator `[]` for map or list element access or insert methods.\n\n## Noncompliant Code\n\n```kotlin\nval map = mutableMapOf<String, String>()\nmap.put(\"key\", \"value\")\nval value = map.get(\"key\")\n```\n## Compliant Code\n\n```kotlin\nval map = mutableMapOf<String, String>()\nmap[\"key\"] = \"value\"\nval value = map[\"key\"]\n```\n\n[Source](https://detekt.dev/docs/rules/style#explicitcollectionelementaccessmethod)",
