    "description" : "This rule enforces consistent indentation for multiline string templates in Kotlin that are post-fixed with .trimIndent(), ensuring the opening and closing triple quotes are on separate lines and the content is aligned with the quotes.",
    "explanation" : "# StringTemplateIndent\n\nEnforce consistent string template indentation for multiline string templates which are post-fixed with `.trimIndent()`. The opening and closing `\"\"\"` are placed on separate lines and the indentation of the content of the template is aligned with the `\"\"\"`.\n\n## Noncompliant Code\n\n```kotlin\n\n    val foo = \"\"\"\n              line1\n              line2\n              \"\"\".trimIndent()\n    fun foo() {\n        return \"\"\"\n            line1\n            line2\n        \"\"\".trimIndent()\n    }\n    \n```\n## Compliant Code\n\n```kotlin\n\n    val foo =\n        \"\"\"\n        line1\n        line2\n        \"\"\".trimIndent()\n    fun foo() {\n        // The opening \"\"\" can not be wrapped to next line as that would result in a compilation error\n        return \"\"\"\n            line1\n            line2\n            \"\"\".trimIndent()\n    }\n    \n```\n\n[Source](https://detekt.dev/docs/rules/formatting#stringtemplateindent)",
