    "description" : "This rule enforces replacing explicit null or empty checks with the idiomatic isNullOrEmpty() call in Kotlin code.",
    "explanation" : "# UseIsNullOrEmpty\n\nThis rule detects null or empty checks that can be replaced with `isNullOrEmpty()` call.\n\n## Noncompliant Code\n\n```kotlin\nfun foo(x: List<Int>?) {\n    if (x == null || x.isEmpty()) return\n}\nfun bar(x: List<Int>?) {\n    if (x == null || x.count() == 0) return\n}\nfun baz(x: List<Int>?) {\n    if (x == null || x.size == 0) return\n}\n```\n## Compliant Code\n\n```kotlin\nif (x.isNullOrEmpty()) return\n```\n\n[Source](https://detekt.dev/docs/rules/style#useisnullorempty)",
